AB  - Endovenous treatment for varicose veins has become increasingly popular over the last decade. Compared to conventional surgery, endovenous options promise lower wound infection rates, less pain and quicker return to normal activities. Treatment modalities can be divided into thermal (EVLT / RFA) or non‐thermal based (Cyanoacrylate glue / MOCA). Literature review has not shown much difference between the two branches of treatment, and there remains a paucity of local data, hence we decided to conduct our own study to investigate the question.
