AB  - Abstract Reflux in the great saphenous vein (GSV) is found in 70% to 80% of patients with chronic venous disease (CVD), which leads to venous hypertension. Open surgery has been replaced by interventions geared towards closing the GSV, which can be grouped into thermal or nonthermal. Radiofrequency ablation (RFA) and endovenous laser therapy (EVLT) using ultrasound-guided tumescent anesthesia placement are discussed herein.
