AB  - Introduction: Varicose veins are a common condition affecting millions worldwide. Cyanoacrylate closure (CAC) and radiofrequency ablation (RFA) are widely used minimally invasive treatments. CAC offers advantages such as eliminating tumescent local anesthesia (TLA) and reducing nerve injury risk. However, there are few reports comparing CAC and RFA outcomes in Japan. This study is aimed at evaluating the efficacy and safety of CAC and RFA for treating great saphenous vein (GSV) and small saphenous vein (SSV) varicose veins.
