AB  - Results: A total of 194 patients with 252 GSVs with an average diameter of 5.7 ± 2.2 mm (range, 2.0 to 18.0 mm) received RSTA under tumescent local anesthesia. In 58 patients (29.9%), bilateral treatment (average length treated, 36.7 ± 10.8 cm) was done. The average total endovenous procedure time was 16.4 ± 8.2 minutes, and the average total energy delivery time was 2.2 ± 0.6 minutes. The corresponding endovenous fluence equivalent delivered to the proximal 7-cm vein segment was 82 ± 25 J/cm2 (range, 38 to 192). Follow-up at 3 days, 3 months, and 6 months was obtained from 250, 164, and 62 limbs, respectively. Occlusion rates were 99.6% for all three follow-up dates according to life-table analysis. The average Venous Clinical Severity Score was 3.4 ± 1.2 at 3 days, 0.9 ± 1.6 at 3 months, and 1.5 ± 1.8 at 6 months compared with 3.9 ± 2.0 at baseline.
